-- =====================================================================
-- RRNetBanking — Slice 1: teardown of the Banking module
--
-- WHY THIS EXISTS
--
-- 'ALTER ENTITY ... DROP ATTRIBUTE' removes the attribute but leaves the
-- validation rule that a NOT NULL created behind, pointing at an
-- attribute that no longer exists. 'mx check' then fails with
--
--   CE1613 "The selected attribute 'Banking.Customer.FullName' no longer
--           exists." at Validation rule of entity 'Banking.Customer'
--
-- and MDL has no statement that can remove a validation rule (no
-- DROP VALIDATION RULE), while DESCRIBE ENTITY does not emit validation
-- rules at all, so the orphan is invisible to a describe/edit/exec
-- round-trip. Rebuilding the entity is the only route back to a clean
-- model with mxcli alone.
--
-- Because Mendix references documents by GUID, everything that points at
-- Banking.Customer has to go with it and be recreated from the slice
-- scripts: recreating an entity under the same qualified name does NOT
-- rebind existing references to it.
--
-- Run order: this script, then s1-01 … s1-06.
-- This is idempotent-ish by design — run it with --continue-on-error, as
-- statements fail harmlessly when the object is already gone.
-- =====================================================================

-- The settings reference has to be cleared before the microflow can go.
ALTER SETTINGS MODEL AfterStartupMicroflow = '';
/

DROP PAGE Banking.Home_Dashboard;
/

DROP MICROFLOW Banking.SCH_AfterStartup;
/
DROP MICROFLOW Banking.SUB_SeedBranches;
/
DROP MICROFLOW Banking.DS_MyAccounts;
/
DROP MICROFLOW Banking.DS_CurrentCustomer;
/

-- Demo users are typed to Banking.Customer, so they block the drop.
DROP DEMO USER 'rahul';
/
DROP DEMO USER 'priya';
/

-- Drop the association before the entity: an association left pointing at
-- a dropped-and-recreated entity keeps the OLD GUID and mxbuild fails with
-- KeyNotFoundException.
DROP ASSOCIATION Banking.Account_Customer;
/

DROP ENTITY Banking.Customer;
/
